  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat → acc 0.527). The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality actually contributes value over an RNA-only model. config_045 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000, no image, no fusion) is the cleanest possible ablation: it matches config_001 on RNA encoder (pca_n2000), profile setting (singleprofile), and removes only the image modality. This isolates the effect of multimodality with a single design change. If config_045 performs comparably to config_001, the image modality is not adding signal and we should redirect budget toward RNA encoder/aggregation choices. If config_045 is substantially worse, the image is valuable and we can confidently invest in multimodal fusion and encoder variations. Establishing this baseline before exploring fusion strategies, multiprofile aggregation, or alternative encoders is the highest-information-use experiment under a limited budget."
}

